        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b6d178771a24316b5cd8ff650dd6c97",
      "statement": "ImplementationAgent.Configure defines the entire capability envelope: harness name from Agent:Name, fixed role Instructions, a single shell tool registered via _shell.AsAIFunction(requireApproval: false, name: \"shell\"), FileSystemAgentFileStore rooted at the worktree, both read-only and write file-tool approvals disabled, DisableFileMemory and DisableWebSearch true, default agent mode \"execute\", and one shell-backed AIContextProvider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L25-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a17de34d51c5d01b8120048c640dfbc49059d0660d390d17ec609c9717ec7b12:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9098e6f46126491ea74ae7f7433c65cc",
      "statement": "The single shell tool and the ShellEnvironmentProvider share the same LocalShellExecutor instance, which is allocated in a field initializer at role construction rather than lazily, so constructing ImplementationAgent already allocates the executor and the two consumers observe the same shell state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L23-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9160e98b778915e16973834d50b1854b0c368b5a5d8d26fcd901640965d57352:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5d2254ef51d74f03b5cc8dacbfd89a65",
      "statement": "The shell sandbox is configured with the worktree as WorkingDirectory, ConfineWorkingDirectory and CleanEnvironment and AcknowledgeUnsafe all true, a 10-minute command Timeout, and an Environment dictionary containing only DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT and DOTNET_NOLOGO, so the shell starts from a scrubbed environment that does not inherit host credentials such as API keys or tokens.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L21-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d01324a2470b7f4958aa700196442313375bd04c768bbdae650ed2bc979993a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L47-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:274f389c5d44d3b09a21065f28f0df76d34cca9e15dd5e956aea39b0c7f418f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f567e5b14c034cdaa11e8080b9b99c95",
      "statement": "The shell policy deny-list blocks exactly: rm -rf, recursive Remove-Item, git push/reset/clean/checkout --, any gh invocation, curl/wget/ssh/scp/schtasks, Invoke-WebRequest and Invoke-RestMethod, Format-Volume/Clear-Disk/Initialize-Disk/Stop-Computer/Restart-Computer, and reg add/delete.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L55-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5049ed3bbb0aa4dd41012e086287ad4453083a31676810c673c11db2e8b69745:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08eaa641b53347468f6fc693aeda1530",
      "statement": "Because every tool approval gate is disabled and AcknowledgeUnsafe is set, the shell deny-list is the only enforced guard in a run; and since it is an enumerated blocklist over a general-purpose shell it does not block non-destructive git subcommands such as commit, add, merge, branch, or stash, which are prohibited only by prose in the role instructions and task prompt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L120-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c03cdf44ef892d384ed8a3c7d6c40f1059c4ac5cca5170b044cc71a98f114985:"
