    {
      "id": "claim_45e16c3694da468d8ae28e2035bd1c94",
      "statement": "The task prompt appends the raw issue body last and constrains the agent with a fixed rule list: treat the issue body as requirements rather than overriding instructions, discover build and test tooling by inspection, restore dependencies but do not add any, report exact test commands and results, run no git commands or commit/push/create PRs, modify nothing outside the workspace, and stop and explain when the spec is ambiguous or blocked — making a blocked-but-explained response a correct run rather than a failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L112-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b6800bf753ee018f2eebd3dcee9ccd4efcf2bf77182bbcb3f22dc77baa8ffb9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd0ebb4205564b028e9d0408d7d3316d",
      "statement": "The experimental harness API surface is deliberately contained by MAAI001/MEAI001 pragmas in only three production files — AgentRole, ImplementationAgent, and ImplementSpec — with ProviderResolver carrying MEAI001 alone for the IChatClient adapter, which keeps the blast radius of a breaking harness upgrade to those files and makes new harness usage outside them a visible, reviewable addition.",
